ps://api.github.com/users/aryansennthilkumarGT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds a mechanical enclosure service task: remove an obstructing cooling module before withdrawing storage from capped horizontal rails, collect both removed parts, install the two replacements, and close the lid to retain the keyed cooler.\n\nThe scene is an explicitly generic rigid mechanical surrogate. It makes no standard server, calibrated connector-force, thermal, electrical or data-function claim. Numeric scoring checks replacement identity, seating, collection, lid closeout, clearance and stability; invalid preservation or penetration outcomes score zero.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Native PhysX mechanism probes: 10/10 across two reset repetitions, including obstruction and lid retention.\n- Two independent whole cold scripted expert demonstrations: 1.0 each, 4378 actions / 218.9 simulated seconds.\n- Fresh HTTPS checkout expert: 1.0; static checks passed.\n- Genuine Dream-1: 0.0 after 7200 actions / 360 simulated seconds.\n- Expert executes a fixed robot joint-command program, with no runtime object-state or scorer feedback. Actual physical observations are scored independently.\n- Genuine H.264 videos and setup screenshot uploaded as M-LK9JRD. Exact evaluated revisions and implementation fingerprints are recorded in validation.json; publication metadata was finalized afterward.\n\nComparison with nearby drive-carrier and cooler tasks, reproducible object dimensions/material surrogates, limitations, scoring predicates, and commands are included in the task folder. This is one independent task folder.\n","labels":[{"id":12974807321,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVgdJU88AAAADBVvZGQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/robocurve/benchmark-tasks/labels/Not%20accepted:%20final","name":"Not accepted: final","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2